      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A force majeure clause generally excuses a tenant's contractual obligations when an unforeseeable event, like a prolonged disruption, makes performance impossible. In Singapore, this clause typically suspends the lease term or payment obligations temporarily, but it does not automatically terminate the lease. Always review the specific wording, as it dictates if the tenant gets relief, if the lease can be terminated, and what procedures must be followed.",
